 "review": "independent read-only review: approve with nits — lend's frame is byte-identical to the crop under presentsWholeSource; no write reaches a lent buffer (every writer and the recorded-write, deferred-copy and flip paths checked with lines); no double free on reachable paths; lend runs only on the render thread, reclaim there or on main after a flush, the deallocator only touches the locked pool; no host mutates frames. Applied before the gate: tiny storages (Data's inline bytes would release a buffer still in use), the doc on lentFrame, an assertion that a lent frame is fully known, a two-buffer pool cap, no wasted copy for a whole overwrite after recorded writes, and tests for those and for releases on other threads. Left: no unit test drives the pipelined present itself (the headless and emulator frame gates and the ThreadSanitizer runs do)"
